@startuml
!include style.puml
title Bounded destructive undo history

state "Live records: C" as C
state "History (oldest to newest): A, B" as AB
state "Live records: D" as D
state "History (oldest to newest): A, B, C" as ABC
state "Live records: C" as C2
state "History (oldest to newest): A, B" as AB2
state "Live records: E" as E
state "History (oldest to newest): A, B, C" as ABC2

C --> D : successful normal change\nappend C after saving
D --> C2 : undo\nsave C, then remove C from history
C2 --> E : successful normal change\nappend C after saving

note right of ABC
The newest snapshot is restored first.
At capacity, the oldest snapshot is discarded
before appending a new predecessor.
end note

note right of AB2
No forward state D is retained.
end note
@enduml
